INSERT INTO sat_questions (question_id, external_id, vault_id, disclosed_item_id, source, program, test_type, test_type_desc, domain, primary_class_cd, skill_cd, skill_desc, difficulty, score_band_range_cd, question_type, stimulus_html, stem_html, answer_options, correct_answer, answer_keys, rationale_html, correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale, image_count, parent_template_name, parent_template_id, template_cluster_id, template_cluster_name, origin, position, answer_style, section, raw_payload, created_date, updated_date) VALUES
    ($SATQ$8d1ddd1b$SATQ$, $SATQ$bc609dfd-b00c-4820-b30b-0bb483974080$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$0adbaec3-2e2a-430d-bb94-458f8fbc353a$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Ducklings expend up to 62.8% less energy when swimming in a line behind their mother than when swimming alone.</li>
<li>The physics behind this energy savings hasn&rsquo;t always been well understood.</li>
<li>Naval architect Zhiming Yuan used computer simulations to study the effect of the mother duck&rsquo;s wake.</li>
<li>The study revealed that ducklings are pushed in a forward direction by the wake&rsquo;s waves.</li>
<li>Yuan determined this push reduces the effect of wave drag on the ducklings by 158%.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to present the study and its methodology. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"da32bf23-90a6-4a65-b520-b69de9d60009","content":"<p>A study revealed that ducklings, which expend up to 62.8% less energy when swimming in a line behind their mother, also experience 158% less drag.</p>"},{"id":"5450daae-6486-4753-b7a8-0e2920fd26d5","content":"<p>Seeking to understand how ducklings swimming in a line behind their mother save energy, Zhiming Yuan used computer simulations to study the effect of the mother duck&rsquo;s wake.</p>"},{"id":"df7ac0e5-aa6a-401a-b1f4-1f92aec62361","content":"<p>Zhiming Yuan studied the physics behind the fact that by being pushed in a forward direction by waves, ducklings save energy.</p>"},{"id":"fe18fe2e-900a-46ed-8d39-3e6b2e19ea83","content":"<p>Naval architect Zhiming Yuan discovered that ducklings are pushed in a forward direction by the waves of their mother&rsquo;s wake, reducing the effect of drag by 158%.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["5450daae-6486-4753-b7a8-0e2920fd26d5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. The sentence presents both the study and its methodology (that is, the researcher&rsquo;s approach to the problem), explaining that Yuan used computer simulations to study the effect of the mother duck&rsquo;s wake on the ducklings&rsquo; energy expenditure. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence describes the findings of Yuan&rsquo;s study; it doesn&rsquo;t present the study and its methodology.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect. While the sentence provides general information about Yuan&rsquo;s study, it doesn&rsquo;t present the study&rsquo;s methodology. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence describes the findings of Yuan&rsquo;s study; it doesn&rsquo;t present the study and its methodology.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-780-SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$5e238567-5b60-49ff-a7dd-57ec87e87033$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"8d1ddd1b","external_id":"bc609dfd-b00c-4820-b30b-0bb483974080","vaultid":"0adbaec3-2e2a-430d-bb94-458f8fbc353a","uId":"c24f2333-a289-4ed0-beab-5945bfdb92ad","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Ducklings expend up to 62.8% less energy when swimming in a line behind their mother than when swimming alone.</li>\n<li>The physics behind this energy savings hasn&rsquo;t always been well understood.</li>\n<li>Naval architect Zhiming Yuan used computer simulations to study the effect of the mother duck&rsquo;s wake.</li>\n<li>The study revealed that ducklings are pushed in a forward direction by the wake&rsquo;s waves.</li>\n<li>Yuan determined this push reduces the effect of wave drag on the ducklings by 158%.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to present the study and its methodology. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"da32bf23-90a6-4a65-b520-b69de9d60009","content":"<p>A study revealed that ducklings, which expend up to 62.8% less energy when swimming in a line behind their mother, also experience 158% less drag.</p>"},{"id":"5450daae-6486-4753-b7a8-0e2920fd26d5","content":"<p>Seeking to understand how ducklings swimming in a line behind their mother save energy, Zhiming Yuan used computer simulations to study the effect of the mother duck&rsquo;s wake.</p>"},{"id":"df7ac0e5-aa6a-401a-b1f4-1f92aec62361","content":"<p>Zhiming Yuan studied the physics behind the fact that by being pushed in a forward direction by waves, ducklings save energy.</p>"},{"id":"fe18fe2e-900a-46ed-8d39-3e6b2e19ea83","content":"<p>Naval architect Zhiming Yuan discovered that ducklings are pushed in a forward direction by the waves of their mother&rsquo;s wake, reducing the effect of drag by 158%.</p>"}],"keys":["5450daae-6486-4753-b7a8-0e2920fd26d5"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. The sentence presents both the study and its methodology (that is, the researcher&rsquo;s approach to the problem), explaining that Yuan used computer simulations to study the effect of the mother duck&rsquo;s wake on the ducklings&rsquo; energy expenditure. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence describes the findings of Yuan&rsquo;s study; it doesn&rsquo;t present the study and its methodology.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect. While the sentence provides general information about Yuan&rsquo;s study, it doesn&rsquo;t present the study&rsquo;s methodology. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence describes the findings of Yuan&rsquo;s study; it doesn&rsquo;t present the study and its methodology.&nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-780-SYN","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"5e238567-5b60-49ff-a7dd-57ec87e87033","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959352,"updateDate":1691007959352}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959352, 1691007959352),
    ($SATQ$8e9677e6$SATQ$, $SATQ$63081b48-0053-4166-9736-642c83892256$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$749d9e40-1886-4b47-aba4-facb4daf55de$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>In 2009, the Craft and Folk Art Museum in Los Angeles hosted a special exhibition, <em>Sue&ntilde;os/Yume,</em> showcasing the works of local sculptor Dora de Larios. As suggested by the show&rsquo;s title (<span lang="es"><em>sue&ntilde;os</em></span> and <span lang="ja"><em>yume</em></span> mean &ldquo;dreams&rdquo; in Spanish and Japanese, respectively), de Larios&rsquo;s art reflects a mix of cultural influences<em>.</em> <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> her work is grounded in the artistic traditions of both Mexico and Japan.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"36f239dd-54f0-452e-9e54-e1c5ae5b2cce","content":"<p>In addition,</p>"},{"id":"76b1f274-902e-4acc-a789-7033872d718a","content":"<p>In contrast,</p>"},{"id":"5e029929-fa20-4823-b794-fdcd10a13298","content":"<p>Specifically,</p>"},{"id":"db7de277-31ce-4e7d-82ad-68fa3a5bca74","content":"<p>Therefore,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["5e029929-fa20-4823-b794-fdcd10a13298"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. &ldquo;Specifically&rdquo; logically signals that this sentence provides specific, precise details elaborating on the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim that de Larios&rsquo;s art reflects a mix of cultures. This sentence specifies which cultures the previous sentence is referring to: the artistic traditions of both Mexico and Japan.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;in addition&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence is a separate point that follows the previous claim about de Larios&rsquo;s art. Instead, it provides specific details elaborating on that claim. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;in contrast&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence contrasts with the previous claim about de Larios&rsquo;s art. Instead, it provides specific details elaborating on that claim.&nbsp;Choice D is incorrect because &ldquo;therefore&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence is a result of the previous claim about de Larios&rsquo;s art. Instead, it provides specific details elaborating on that claim. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-253-TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$718ae951-cdb9-4398-a1d0-225ac572afeb$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"8e9677e6","external_id":"63081b48-0053-4166-9736-642c83892256","vaultid":"749d9e40-1886-4b47-aba4-facb4daf55de","uId":"41d61e01-3c04-490a-a440-48820cb5a930","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>In 2009, the Craft and Folk Art Museum in Los Angeles hosted a special exhibition, <em>Sue&ntilde;os/Yume,</em> showcasing the works of local sculptor Dora de Larios. As suggested by the show&rsquo;s title (<span lang=\"es\"><em>sue&ntilde;os</em></span> and <span lang=\"ja\"><em>yume</em></span> mean &ldquo;dreams&rdquo; in Spanish and Japanese, respectively), de Larios&rsquo;s art reflects a mix of cultural influences<em>.</em> <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> her work is grounded in the artistic traditions of both Mexico and Japan.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"36f239dd-54f0-452e-9e54-e1c5ae5b2cce","content":"<p>In addition,</p>"},{"id":"76b1f274-902e-4acc-a789-7033872d718a","content":"<p>In contrast,</p>"},{"id":"5e029929-fa20-4823-b794-fdcd10a13298","content":"<p>Specifically,</p>"},{"id":"db7de277-31ce-4e7d-82ad-68fa3a5bca74","content":"<p>Therefore,</p>"}],"keys":["5e029929-fa20-4823-b794-fdcd10a13298"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. &ldquo;Specifically&rdquo; logically signals that this sentence provides specific, precise details elaborating on the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim that de Larios&rsquo;s art reflects a mix of cultures. This sentence specifies which cultures the previous sentence is referring to: the artistic traditions of both Mexico and Japan.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;in addition&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence is a separate point that follows the previous claim about de Larios&rsquo;s art. Instead, it provides specific details elaborating on that claim. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;in contrast&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence contrasts with the previous claim about de Larios&rsquo;s art. Instead, it provides specific details elaborating on that claim.&nbsp;Choice D is incorrect because &ldquo;therefore&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence is a result of the previous claim about de Larios&rsquo;s art. Instead, it provides specific details elaborating on that claim. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-253-TRA","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"718ae951-cdb9-4398-a1d0-225ac572afeb","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959333,"updateDate":1691007959333}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959333, 1691007959333),
    ($SATQ$8fe4f4ab$SATQ$, $SATQ$ab40fd7d-4d0a-4e63-a40b-8530b5444a6a$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$e358728f-5628-4f4b-8a80-618e397bd97f$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>One of history&rsquo;s greatest libraries was the House of Wisdom in Baghdad, Iraq.</li>
<li>It was founded in the eighth century with the goal of preserving all the world&rsquo;s knowledge.</li>
<li>Scholars at the House of Wisdom collected ancient and contemporary texts from Greece, India, and elsewhere and translated them into Arabic.</li>
<li>Writings included those of the Greek philosopher Aristotle and the Indian mathematician Aryabhata.</li>
<li>The House of Wisdom used Chinese papermaking technology to create paper versions to be studied and shared.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to explain how the House of Wisdom preserved the world&rsquo;s knowledge. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"2a4f1508-d1e5-4b74-85e1-0efca636165d","content":"<p>The House of Wisdom was known for bringing together knowledge from around the world, including from Greece, India, and China.</p>"},{"id":"aca7fdeb-b91c-41ce-a940-ffa5443dd12b","content":"<p>Founded in Iraq in the eighth century, the House of Wisdom employed many scholars as translators.</p>"},{"id":"64ca53e8-4672-4a5a-8627-01819096e44d","content":"<p>Writings from the Greek philosopher Aristotle and the Indian mathematician Aryabhata were preserved at the House of Wisdom.</p>"},{"id":"2fd6ea07-1c50-4728-87e8-8f7d1f991d72","content":"<p>The House of Wisdom collected writings from different countries and created paper versions in Arabic to be studied and shared.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["2fd6ea07-1c50-4728-87e8-8f7d1f991d72"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. The sentence explains how the House of Wisdom preserved the world&rsquo;s knowledge, noting that the library collected, translated, and printed writings from different countries.&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. While the sentence indicates that the House of Wisdom was known for bringing together knowledge from around the world, it doesn&rsquo;t explain how the library preserved this knowledge. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence makes a generalization about the scholars who were employed by the House of Wisdom; it doesn&rsquo;t explain how the library preserved the world&rsquo;s knowledge. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence identifies two authors whose writings were preserved at the House of Wisdom; it doesn&rsquo;t explain how the library preserved the world&rsquo;s knowledge. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-753-SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$fac08ea0-1494-47b7-8547-b8f123fb85df$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"8fe4f4ab","external_id":"ab40fd7d-4d0a-4e63-a40b-8530b5444a6a","vaultid":"e358728f-5628-4f4b-8a80-618e397bd97f","uId":"2e20d929-d3d2-4c38-b6c9-dd7a1a95aa5e","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>One of history&rsquo;s greatest libraries was the House of Wisdom in Baghdad, Iraq.</li>\n<li>It was founded in the eighth century with the goal of preserving all the world&rsquo;s knowledge.</li>\n<li>Scholars at the House of Wisdom collected ancient and contemporary texts from Greece, India, and elsewhere and translated them into Arabic.</li>\n<li>Writings included those of the Greek philosopher Aristotle and the Indian mathematician Aryabhata.</li>\n<li>The House of Wisdom used Chinese papermaking technology to create paper versions to be studied and shared.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to explain how the House of Wisdom preserved the world&rsquo;s knowledge. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"2a4f1508-d1e5-4b74-85e1-0efca636165d","content":"<p>The House of Wisdom was known for bringing together knowledge from around the world, including from Greece, India, and China.</p>"},{"id":"aca7fdeb-b91c-41ce-a940-ffa5443dd12b","content":"<p>Founded in Iraq in the eighth century, the House of Wisdom employed many scholars as translators.</p>"},{"id":"64ca53e8-4672-4a5a-8627-01819096e44d","content":"<p>Writings from the Greek philosopher Aristotle and the Indian mathematician Aryabhata were preserved at the House of Wisdom.</p>"},{"id":"2fd6ea07-1c50-4728-87e8-8f7d1f991d72","content":"<p>The House of Wisdom collected writings from different countries and created paper versions in Arabic to be studied and shared.</p>"}],"keys":["2fd6ea07-1c50-4728-87e8-8f7d1f991d72"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. The sentence explains how the House of Wisdom preserved the world&rsquo;s knowledge, noting that the library collected, translated, and printed writings from different countries.&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. While the sentence indicates that the House of Wisdom was known for bringing together knowledge from around the world, it doesn&rsquo;t explain how the library preserved this knowledge. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence makes a generalization about the scholars who were employed by the House of Wisdom; it doesn&rsquo;t explain how the library preserved the world&rsquo;s knowledge. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence identifies two authors whose writings were preserved at the House of Wisdom; it doesn&rsquo;t explain how the library preserved the world&rsquo;s knowledge. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-753-SYN","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"fac08ea0-1494-47b7-8547-b8f123fb85df","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959350,"updateDate":1691007959350}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959350, 1691007959350),
    ($SATQ$90117366$SATQ$, $SATQ$7cb902b9-8d7e-4cdb-b081-96c1113c4978$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$2de964b9-42a2-4b00-9d40-62102cff0e3d$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>To explore how blinking affects social interactions, Dutch researchers observed interactions between human speakers and &ldquo;listeners&rdquo; (animated human faces on a screen). The researchers found that when the listeners blinked slowly, the speakers tended to talk for less time. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> quicker blinks were associated with longer talking times.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"9da19e18-f0fe-41d3-947a-f2090d1abc19","content":"<p>For example,</p>"},{"id":"dfdf54e1-3677-4201-a2c2-78b33143c21f","content":"<p>Specifically,</p>"},{"id":"6ed4ddba-1950-4557-afe0-8a4ba6d6112f","content":"<p>Firstly,</p>"},{"id":"677b1b7c-3ade-44e0-994c-845e71a682c4","content":"<p>By contrast,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["677b1b7c-3ade-44e0-994c-845e71a682c4"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. &ldquo;By contrast&rdquo; logically signals that the finding described in this sentence contrasts with the finding described in the previous sentence. That is, quicker blinks were associated with longer talking times, whereas slower blinks were associated with shorter talking times.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;for example&rdquo; illogically signals that the finding described in this sentence is an example of the finding described in the previous sentence. Instead, it contrasts with that finding. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;specifically&rdquo; illogically signals that this sentence provides specific, precise details about the finding described in the previous sentence. Instead, it presents information that contrasts with that finding.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;firstly&rdquo; illogically signals that the finding described in this sentence is a first point or occurs first in a chronological sequence of events. Instead, it contrasts with the finding described in the previous sentence.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-249-TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$48ff0fcc-251e-4ad2-bd80-25671c125fec$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"90117366","external_id":"7cb902b9-8d7e-4cdb-b081-96c1113c4978","vaultid":"2de964b9-42a2-4b00-9d40-62102cff0e3d","uId":"ca9e0086-8f5e-434f-897a-98c62f48b895","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>To explore how blinking affects social interactions, Dutch researchers observed interactions between human speakers and &ldquo;listeners&rdquo; (animated human faces on a screen). The researchers found that when the listeners blinked slowly, the speakers tended to talk for less time. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> quicker blinks were associated with longer talking times.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"9da19e18-f0fe-41d3-947a-f2090d1abc19","content":"<p>For example,</p>"},{"id":"dfdf54e1-3677-4201-a2c2-78b33143c21f","content":"<p>Specifically,</p>"},{"id":"6ed4ddba-1950-4557-afe0-8a4ba6d6112f","content":"<p>Firstly,</p>"},{"id":"677b1b7c-3ade-44e0-994c-845e71a682c4","content":"<p>By contrast,</p>"}],"keys":["677b1b7c-3ade-44e0-994c-845e71a682c4"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. &ldquo;By contrast&rdquo; logically signals that the finding described in this sentence contrasts with the finding described in the previous sentence. That is, quicker blinks were associated with longer talking times, whereas slower blinks were associated with shorter talking times.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;for example&rdquo; illogically signals that the finding described in this sentence is an example of the finding described in the previous sentence. Instead, it contrasts with that finding. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;specifically&rdquo; illogically signals that this sentence provides specific, precise details about the finding described in the previous sentence. Instead, it presents information that contrasts with that finding.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;firstly&rdquo; illogically signals that the finding described in this sentence is a first point or occurs first in a chronological sequence of events. Instead, it contrasts with the finding described in the previous sentence.&nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-249-TRA","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"48ff0fcc-251e-4ad2-bd80-25671c125fec","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959333,"updateDate":1691007959333}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959333, 1691007959333),
    ($SATQ$911c7a87$SATQ$, $SATQ$f57f6c2a-a76e-40ae-8c7c-ae65f8ba8b81$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>After appropriate permissions are granted, a typical archaeological dig begins with a surveyor making a detailed grid of the excavation site. Then, the site is carefully dug, and any artifacts found are recorded and mapped onto the site grid. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> the artifacts are removed, cataloged, and analyzed in a laboratory.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"3b9dff7c-8083-4077-8fd8-932c3fbfeb70","content":"<p>For instance,</p>"},{"id":"f705ec09-9c95-4bff-bb01-8d825509456d","content":"<p>On the contrary,</p>"},{"id":"f2db603a-392a-461b-95a6-23094a13e435","content":"<p>Earlier,</p>"},{"id":"37c7467f-77d5-4a8f-b08c-69fea668c9ab","content":"<p>Finally,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["37c7467f-77d5-4a8f-b08c-69fea668c9ab"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. "Finally" logically signals that the actions in this sentence&mdash;the removal, cataloging, and analysis of artifacts&mdash;are the next and final steps in a process, following the previous actions of surveying, digging, recording, and mapping.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because "for instance" illogically signals that the actions in this sentence are an example of the actions in the previous sentence. Instead, the removal, cataloging, and analysis of artifacts are the next and final steps in a process. Choice B is incorrect because "on the contrary" illogically signals that the actions in this sentence are directly opposed to the actions in the previous sentence. Instead, the removal, cataloging, and analysis of artifacts are the next and final steps in a process. Choice C is incorrect because "earlier" illogically signals that the actions in this sentence occur before the actions in the previous sentence. Instead, the removal, cataloging, and analysis of artifacts are the next and final steps in a process.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"911c7a87","external_id":"f57f6c2a-a76e-40ae-8c7c-ae65f8ba8b81","vaultid":null,"uId":"5e6c3d9e-6914-47cc-92c4-62a26e2d74e0","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>After appropriate permissions are granted, a typical archaeological dig begins with a surveyor making a detailed grid of the excavation site. Then, the site is carefully dug, and any artifacts found are recorded and mapped onto the site grid. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> the artifacts are removed, cataloged, and analyzed in a laboratory.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"3b9dff7c-8083-4077-8fd8-932c3fbfeb70","content":"<p>For instance,</p>"},{"id":"f705ec09-9c95-4bff-bb01-8d825509456d","content":"<p>On the contrary,</p>"},{"id":"f2db603a-392a-461b-95a6-23094a13e435","content":"<p>Earlier,</p>"},{"id":"37c7467f-77d5-4a8f-b08c-69fea668c9ab","content":"<p>Finally,</p>"}],"keys":["37c7467f-77d5-4a8f-b08c-69fea668c9ab"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. \"Finally\" logically signals that the actions in this sentence&mdash;the removal, cataloging, and analysis of artifacts&mdash;are the next and final steps in a process, following the previous actions of surveying, digging, recording, and mapping.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because \"for instance\" illogically signals that the actions in this sentence are an example of the actions in the previous sentence. Instead, the removal, cataloging, and analysis of artifacts are the next and final steps in a process. Choice B is incorrect because \"on the contrary\" illogically signals that the actions in this sentence are directly opposed to the actions in the previous sentence. Instead, the removal, cataloging, and analysis of artifacts are the next and final steps in a process. Choice C is incorrect because \"earlier\" illogically signals that the actions in this sentence occur before the actions in the previous sentence. Instead, the removal, cataloging, and analysis of artifacts are the next and final steps in a process.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323043,"updateDate":1730147323043}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323043, 1730147323043),
    ($SATQ$92dec236$SATQ$, $SATQ$8088ce8e-5fa4-4a27-873e-7ca9d15f2a00$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$d7377cb6-a3da-4b7e-be85-f00692be2da8$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Maika&rsquo;i Tubbs is a Native Hawaiian sculptor and installation artist.</li>
<li>His work has been shown in the United States, Canada, Japan, and Germany, among other places.</li>
<li>Many of his sculptures feature discarded objects.</li>
<li>His work <em>Erasure </em>(2008) includes discarded audiocassette tapes and magnets.</li>
<li>His work <em>Home Grown </em>(2009) includes discarded pushpins, plastic plates and forks, and wood.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity between the two works. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"1dba2141-ecc8-4e4b-a609-9f11b0bda666","content":"<p><em>Erasure</em> (2008) uses discarded objects such as audiocassette tapes and magnets; <em>Home Grown</em> (2009), however, includes pushpins, plastic plates and forks, and wood.</p>"},{"id":"f72d90dc-6cb2-4c62-9cef-9aad84ae92cd","content":"<p>Tubbs&rsquo;s work, which often features discarded objects, has been shown both within the United States and abroad.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"6c245ad9-9dc5-4d32-8092-7fc97287e680","content":"<p>Like many of Tubbs&rsquo;s sculptures, both <em>Erasure </em>and <em>Home Grown</em> include discarded objects: <em>Erasure </em>uses audiocassette tapes, and <em>Home Grown </em>uses plastic forks.</p>"},{"id":"722b97a4-75d3-452e-a20a-db1dda40b897","content":"<p>Tubbs completed <em>Erasure </em>in 2008 and <em>Home Grown</em> in 2009.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["6c245ad9-9dc5-4d32-8092-7fc97287e680"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. This choice most effectively emphasizes "a similarity" by identifying a trait the works share: "both Erasure and Home Grown include discarded objects."</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t "emphasize a similarity." Instead, this choice shows how the materials used in the two works are different. Notice the use of the contrast word "however." Choice B is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t "emphasize a similarity between the two works." While it says that Tubbs&rsquo;s work "often features discarded objects," it doesn&rsquo;t provide details about the two works in question. Choice D is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t "emphasize a similarity." Instead, this choice shows how the works were produced at different times.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-700-SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$96835b85-9088-4990-97aa-0a3f7eec34e3$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"92dec236","external_id":"8088ce8e-5fa4-4a27-873e-7ca9d15f2a00","vaultid":"d7377cb6-a3da-4b7e-be85-f00692be2da8","uId":"fbe292f7-ca0c-4117-ad96-dfcb3b51f57f","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Maika&rsquo;i Tubbs is a Native Hawaiian sculptor and installation artist.</li>\n<li>His work has been shown in the United States, Canada, Japan, and Germany, among other places.</li>\n<li>Many of his sculptures feature discarded objects.</li>\n<li>His work <em>Erasure </em>(2008) includes discarded audiocassette tapes and magnets.</li>\n<li>His work <em>Home Grown </em>(2009) includes discarded pushpins, plastic plates and forks, and wood.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity between the two works. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"1dba2141-ecc8-4e4b-a609-9f11b0bda666","content":"<p><em>Erasure</em> (2008) uses discarded objects such as audiocassette tapes and magnets; <em>Home Grown</em> (2009), however, includes pushpins, plastic plates and forks, and wood.</p>"},{"id":"f72d90dc-6cb2-4c62-9cef-9aad84ae92cd","content":"<p>Tubbs&rsquo;s work, which often features discarded objects, has been shown both within the United States and abroad.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"6c245ad9-9dc5-4d32-8092-7fc97287e680","content":"<p>Like many of Tubbs&rsquo;s sculptures, both <em>Erasure </em>and <em>Home Grown</em> include discarded objects: <em>Erasure </em>uses audiocassette tapes, and <em>Home Grown </em>uses plastic forks.</p>"},{"id":"722b97a4-75d3-452e-a20a-db1dda40b897","content":"<p>Tubbs completed <em>Erasure </em>in 2008 and <em>Home Grown</em> in 2009.</p>"}],"keys":["6c245ad9-9dc5-4d32-8092-7fc97287e680"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. This choice most effectively emphasizes \"a similarity\" by identifying a trait the works share: \"both Erasure and Home Grown include discarded objects.\"</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t \"emphasize a similarity.\" Instead, this choice shows how the materials used in the two works are different. Notice the use of the contrast word \"however.\" Choice B is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t \"emphasize a similarity between the two works.\" While it says that Tubbs&rsquo;s work \"often features discarded objects,\" it doesn&rsquo;t provide details about the two works in question. Choice D is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t \"emphasize a similarity.\" Instead, this choice shows how the works were produced at different times.</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-700-SYN","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"96835b85-9088-4990-97aa-0a3f7eec34e3","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959347,"updateDate":1691007959347}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959347, 1691007959347),
    ($SATQ$92fe0ed7$SATQ$, $SATQ$89811cb9-4ffc-4f17-ae1e-6a4d768e9c0a$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$57c6eca3-8646-4e4b-8ae4-e0b635748733$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Geoscientists have long considered Hawaii&rsquo;s Mauna Loa volcano to be Earth&rsquo;s largest shield volcano by volume, measuring approximately 74,000 cubic kilometers. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> according to a 2020 study by local geoscientist Michael Garcia, Hawaii&rsquo;s Pūhāhonu shield volcano is significantly larger, boasting a volume of about 148,000 cubic kilometers.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"9494d4db-656f-4cac-9dbf-173907b14b47","content":"<p>Secondly,</p>"},{"id":"ab8439ef-7eeb-411d-819b-e5d8fc67bac3","content":"<p>Consequently,</p>"},{"id":"5db3ca92-fd04-4c90-ae8e-b4b2d11e8411","content":"<p>Moreover,</p>"},{"id":"9c1b8459-91ce-4a20-913d-df98c3ba3343","content":"<p>However,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["9c1b8459-91ce-4a20-913d-df98c3ba3343"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. &ldquo;However&rdquo; logically signals that this sentence, which indicates that the Pūhāhonu volcano may be larger than the Mauna Loa volcano, offers a contrast to or refutation of the previous assumption that Mauna Loa is the largest shield volcano. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;secondly&rdquo; illogically signals that this sentence merely offers an additional or secondary point concerning the previous assumption that Mauna Loa is the largest shield volcano. Instead, the sentence offers a contrast to or refutation of that assumption. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;consequently&rdquo; illogically signals that this sentence offers a result or consequence of the previous assumption that Mauna Loa is the largest shield volcano. Instead, the sentence offers a contrast to or refutation of that assumption. Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;moreover&rdquo; illogically signals that this sentence merely adds to the previous assumption that Mauna Loa is the largest shield volcano. Instead, the sentence offers a contrast to or refutation of that assumption. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-216-TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$8bb3ba7d-3a9c-44b4-9c4b-3ac40365dbd7$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"92fe0ed7","external_id":"89811cb9-4ffc-4f17-ae1e-6a4d768e9c0a","vaultid":"57c6eca3-8646-4e4b-8ae4-e0b635748733","uId":"2080c38a-d86f-4c7c-aed6-1b390fda4f30","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Geoscientists have long considered Hawaii&rsquo;s Mauna Loa volcano to be Earth&rsquo;s largest shield volcano by volume, measuring approximately 74,000 cubic kilometers. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> according to a 2020 study by local geoscientist Michael Garcia, Hawaii&rsquo;s Pūhāhonu shield volcano is significantly larger, boasting a volume of about 148,000 cubic kilometers.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"9494d4db-656f-4cac-9dbf-173907b14b47","content":"<p>Secondly,</p>"},{"id":"ab8439ef-7eeb-411d-819b-e5d8fc67bac3","content":"<p>Consequently,</p>"},{"id":"5db3ca92-fd04-4c90-ae8e-b4b2d11e8411","content":"<p>Moreover,</p>"},{"id":"9c1b8459-91ce-4a20-913d-df98c3ba3343","content":"<p>However,</p>"}],"keys":["9c1b8459-91ce-4a20-913d-df98c3ba3343"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. &ldquo;However&rdquo; logically signals that this sentence, which indicates that the Pūhāhonu volcano may be larger than the Mauna Loa volcano, offers a contrast to or refutation of the previous assumption that Mauna Loa is the largest shield volcano. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;secondly&rdquo; illogically signals that this sentence merely offers an additional or secondary point concerning the previous assumption that Mauna Loa is the largest shield volcano. Instead, the sentence offers a contrast to or refutation of that assumption. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;consequently&rdquo; illogically signals that this sentence offers a result or consequence of the previous assumption that Mauna Loa is the largest shield volcano. Instead, the sentence offers a contrast to or refutation of that assumption. Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;moreover&rdquo; illogically signals that this sentence merely adds to the previous assumption that Mauna Loa is the largest shield volcano. Instead, the sentence offers a contrast to or refutation of that assumption. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-216-TRA","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"8bb3ba7d-3a9c-44b4-9c4b-3ac40365dbd7","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959327,"updateDate":1691007959327}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959327, 1691007959327),
    ($SATQ$9336f63b$SATQ$, $SATQ$e4051f7d-72b1-4839-919f-d942b9f73ba4$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>A small number of US Navy sailors of Filipino descent served during the US Civil War (1861&ndash;1865).</li>
<li>Stephen Amos was born in the Philippines around 1830.</li>
<li>He enlisted in the US Navy in November 1863.</li>
<li>Raphael Ignases was born in the Philippines around 1834.</li>
<li>He enlisted in the US Navy in July 1861.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize the historical significance of Stephen Amos&rsquo;s enlistment date. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"1bd20020-4293-4639-906b-e7071997910d","content":"<p>Both Stephen Amos and Raphael Ignases were US Navy sailors of Filipino descent, but Amos enlisted in the Navy in 1863, two years later than Ignases.</p>"},{"id":"0d33a2bd-290b-4059-9254-6ab74e046748","content":"<p>Stephen Amos was a US Navy sailor of Filipino descent, along with Raphael Ignases, who was born in the Philippines around 1834.</p>"},{"id":"27073972-3942-4b71-8f01-31166b0c04e8","content":"<p>Stephen Amos enlisted in the US Navy in 1863, making him one of the few sailors of Filipino descent to serve in the US Civil War (1861&ndash;1865).</p>"},{"id":"92055e5e-e49b-4412-b9b8-d2c02e5560cc","content":"<p>When Stephen Amos enlisted in the US Navy in November 1863, he joined sailors such as Raphael Ignases, who had been born in the Philippines around 1834.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["27073972-3942-4b71-8f01-31166b0c04e8"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. Noting the time frame of the US Civil War and the fact that Amos enlisted during this time frame, the sentence emphasizes that Amos&rsquo;s enlistment date places him among the historically significant group of US Navy sailors of Filipino descent who served during the Civil War.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence identifies Amos and Ignases and notes that Amos&rsquo;s enlistment date was later than Ignases&rsquo;s; the sentence doesn&rsquo;t explain the historical significance of the date. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence identifies Amos and Ignases as US Navy sailors of Filipino descent, noting Ignases&rsquo;s birth year; the sentence doesn&rsquo;t provide Amos&rsquo;s enlistment date or its historical significance. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence provides Amos&rsquo;s enlistment date and mentions that he served alongside a sailor of Filipino descent; it doesn&rsquo;t explain the historical significance of the date.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"9336f63b","external_id":"e4051f7d-72b1-4839-919f-d942b9f73ba4","vaultid":null,"uId":"8409824f-3b01-4896-b88b-4b4052fbff3b","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A small number of US Navy sailors of Filipino descent served during the US Civil War (1861&ndash;1865).</li>\n<li>Stephen Amos was born in the Philippines around 1830.</li>\n<li>He enlisted in the US Navy in November 1863.</li>\n<li>Raphael Ignases was born in the Philippines around 1834.</li>\n<li>He enlisted in the US Navy in July 1861.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to emphasize the historical significance of Stephen Amos&rsquo;s enlistment date. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"1bd20020-4293-4639-906b-e7071997910d","content":"<p>Both Stephen Amos and Raphael Ignases were US Navy sailors of Filipino descent, but Amos enlisted in the Navy in 1863, two years later than Ignases.</p>"},{"id":"0d33a2bd-290b-4059-9254-6ab74e046748","content":"<p>Stephen Amos was a US Navy sailor of Filipino descent, along with Raphael Ignases, who was born in the Philippines around 1834.</p>"},{"id":"27073972-3942-4b71-8f01-31166b0c04e8","content":"<p>Stephen Amos enlisted in the US Navy in 1863, making him one of the few sailors of Filipino descent to serve in the US Civil War (1861&ndash;1865).</p>"},{"id":"92055e5e-e49b-4412-b9b8-d2c02e5560cc","content":"<p>When Stephen Amos enlisted in the US Navy in November 1863, he joined sailors such as Raphael Ignases, who had been born in the Philippines around 1834.</p>"}],"keys":["27073972-3942-4b71-8f01-31166b0c04e8"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. Noting the time frame of the US Civil War and the fact that Amos enlisted during this time frame, the sentence emphasizes that Amos&rsquo;s enlistment date places him among the historically significant group of US Navy sailors of Filipino descent who served during the Civil War.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence identifies Amos and Ignases and notes that Amos&rsquo;s enlistment date was later than Ignases&rsquo;s; the sentence doesn&rsquo;t explain the historical significance of the date. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence identifies Amos and Ignases as US Navy sailors of Filipino descent, noting Ignases&rsquo;s birth year; the sentence doesn&rsquo;t provide Amos&rsquo;s enlistment date or its historical significance. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence provides Amos&rsquo;s enlistment date and mentions that he served alongside a sailor of Filipino descent; it doesn&rsquo;t explain the historical significance of the date.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323032,"updateDate":1730147323032}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323032, 1730147323032),
    ($SATQ$94cb8720$SATQ$, $SATQ$d3231009-cffa-4032-99f1-3ae0a8c3c952$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$1b3bdd9a-5d38-49c5-805a-f00095842004$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>In 2020, theater students at Radford and Virginia Tech chose an interactive, online format to present a play about woman suffrage activists.</li>
<li>Their &ldquo;Women and the Vote&rdquo; website featured an interactive digital drawing of a Victorian-style house.</li>
<li>Audiences were asked to focus on a room of their choice and select from that room an artifact related to the suffrage movement.</li>
<li>One click took them to video clips, songs, artwork, and texts associated with the artifact.</li>
<li>The play was popular with audiences because the format allowed them to control the experience.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to explain an advantage of the &ldquo;Women and the Vote&rdquo; format. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal? </p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"d761eeb4-c7f3-4cb6-aedf-752b6e097272","content":"<p>&ldquo;Women and the Vote&rdquo; featured a drawing of a Victorian-style house with several rooms, each containing suffrage artifacts.</p>"},{"id":"601e2ef6-f5c7-43aa-a22b-24c9b1e4b102","content":"<p>To access video clips, songs, artwork, and texts, audiences had to first click on an artifact.</p>"},{"id":"69917baa-c605-47f9-90da-3addf2099e37","content":"<p>The &ldquo;Women and the Vote&rdquo; format appealed to audiences because it allowed them to control the experience. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"370fc029-5697-459e-a7ad-ed3fe8acc29d","content":"<p>Using an interactive format, theater students at Radford and Virginia Tech created &ldquo;Women and the Vote,&rdquo; a play about woman suffrage activists.&nbsp;</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["69917baa-c605-47f9-90da-3addf2099e37"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. The sentence explains an advantage of the &ldquo;Women and the Vote&rdquo; format, noting that the format appealed to audiences because it allowed them to control the experience. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence describes a digital drawing on the &ldquo;Women and the Vote&rdquo; website; it doesn&rsquo;t explain an advantage of the play&rsquo;s format. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence explains how audiences interacted with the &ldquo;Women and the Vote&rdquo; website; it doesn&rsquo;t explain an advantage of the play&rsquo;s format. Choice D is incorrect. While the sentence mentions that &ldquo;Women and the Vote&rdquo; had an interactive format, it doesn&rsquo;t explain what advantage this format might have.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-781-SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$ea11cf1a-b2af-4a55-8547-2fd4606e0133$SATQ$::uui